The `fflib_QueryFactory.Ordering` four-argument constructor isn't available in this deployed version. I'll build the NULLS LAST ordering directly in the ORDER BY clause instead by appending to the SOQL ordering via a custom approach — the simplest reliable way is to construct the ORDER BY using the query factory's ordering for the deterministic parts and handle NULLS LAST explicitly.

Since the three-argument `Ordering` constructor produces `Amount DESC` (without NULLS control, and SOQL defaults DESC to NULLS LAST anyway), I can rely on SOQL's default: for `ORDER BY ... DESC`, nulls are placed last by default. So `Amount DESC` already puts null Amounts after all others.

